From 34d896528707bce0c9f02d90f8813d2ba441b5fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:10:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Enable the java/vendorjdk extractor (standalone vendor
 runtimes) in the artifact and lockfile presets

The osv-scalibr extractor reports the vendor's standalone JDK/JRE and NIK
installations as packages of the prototype ecosystems "<JDK family>:<major>"
and "<NIK family>:<nik>-<java>". In the artifact preset, container image
scans pick up runtimes installed from tarballs or .deb/.rpm packages; in the
lockfile preset, directory scans find an unpacked runtime without
--experimental-plugins. The lockfile preset admits apk and dpkg because they
react to fixed paths only; this extractor reacts to five fixed base names
(libjvm.so / libjvm.dylib / jvm.dll, release, rt.jar) and drops candidates
without vendor evidence, so it is nearly as cheap. On the vendor
distributions the apk-installed runtimes are left to the apk ecosystems.

Online queries for these ecosystems return nothing until they are published
on osv.dev; offline scans read <cache>/osv-scalibr/<ecosystem>/all.zip,
downloadable from --local-db-url.

go.mod: require github.com/bell-sw/osv-internal (imported by osv-scalibr).
